And I'm thinking about\u2014 I don't think that's true. I don't think that's true at all. I think that's just flying a girl in that you're having a relationship."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["humor", "sarcasm", "social media", "public opinion", "exposing scandals", "celebrity gossip", "katt williams", "diddy", "jail", "sex trafficking", "legal definition", "interstate travel", "criminal law", "entertainment industry", "consent", "misinformation", "relationships", "regulation"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778713562.9837635, "duration_sec": 1.681859016418457, "validator_hotkey": "5HNe4Yx7idMcgrsoPogLVko2AA8Pap33aNyXQhpwBxsS4H4Q", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Yeah. I'll extend that even further and say that your knowledge bank is not just limited to your technology skills, right? What you're doing in your hobbies and painting miniatures, that knowledge in some way that perhaps we can't really access or understand is going to play into the rest of your knowledge, right? It gives you a..."], [0, "broader range of things to pull from, a broader range of models to pull from to understand the world. And just because it's not code, right? Just because, you know, whatever you want to say is separate, it's out in this other world, doesn't mean that it's not going to make you a more kind of capable person, a more capable engineer."], [0, "Yeah, totally. And, you know, there are other things in my life that I can look back on that really helped build kind of the business be successful. I've worked in, I've had some pretty crappy jobs in my career. You know, I've worked for some people that I wouldn't consider good bosses, but all of that time that I spent with them really helped me hone in what not to do."], [0, "When I started a business, when we started hiring people, I learned very, very quickly what I shouldn't be doing based off my, my experience in the past of having bad bosses. And so if you've got a bad boss now, one day you will lose, you will use those learnings. When you start managing people, you'll remember that. I remember that time that my boss did that thing. Yeah. I won't do that again."], [0, "Yeah, yeah. I mean, with things like a hobby or with things like a previous job that has nothing to do with this industry, you learn kind of these meta skills, right? You might, for example, I'm just kind of making this up, but you might learn the importance of patience with painting."], [0, "You know, I screwed this up, but it's resilience. You might also learn how resilient the things that you're working with can be, that you can repaint that particular portion or that it's easy to start over, that you can wash things off."], [0, "Again, I'm kind of extending the metaphor a little bit further than perhaps it has the legs to go. But this is the kind of thinking, though, that integrated learning experience that we can have, that everything plays into everything else. And I do think that those small experiences make us a more complete version, a better thinker than we would otherwise be."], [0, "Thank you so much for listening to today's episode of developer T the first part of my interview with the CTO and co-founder of build kite. Go and find out more about what build kite does and what it can do for your company at build kite.com. Build kite did not sponsor this episode and has not sponsored developer T in the past."], [0, "Thank you so much for listening to today's episode. Today's episode was sponsored by Linode. Head over to linode.com slash developer T. You can get $100 worth of free credit by using that specific link. That's linode.com slash developer T. This episode and every other episode of developer T can be found at spec.fm. And this episode was produced by Sarah Jackson. My name is Jonathan Cottrell. Make sure you subscribe so you don't miss out on the second part of this interview. And until next time,"], [0, "Enjoy your tea."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["technology skills", "hobbies", "painting miniatures", "knowledge bank", "learning", "engineering", "business success", "career experience", "bad bosses", "management", "patience", "resilience", "leadership", "hiring", "mentorship", "entrepreneurship", "cloud hosting", "software tools"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
